I reminded Mom of that January morning.
"Mom, I woke up very early that day," I said.
"Yes, and you put some final clothes in your bag," Mom said.
"Then I closed my big suitcase," I said.
"We all sat in the car," Mom said.
"And we went to the airport," I continued.
Mom smiled and said, "We stopped at the big gate of the airport."
"There I hugged Diego and Sofia," I said.
"You hugged Papa too," Mom remembered.
"Yes, and I hugged you for a long time," I said.
"I cried a lot," Mom said.
"I cried too," I said, "but then I wiped my tears."
"You lovingly said goodbye to us," Mom said.
"And I went inside the airport," I said.
"When you turned back and looked, I cried again," Mom said.
"That day was very difficult, Mom," I said.
Mom said, "Yes Maya, but today you are very happy in Mumbai."
